-- title:
--   Finiteness and fibre rank m of Γ(V)/(g)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring (in universe $u$), let $C$ be a scheme and $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ a proper morphism which is smooth of relative dimension $1$. Let $\varepsilon$ be a morphism over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ from $\operatorname{Spec} R$ to $C$ relative to the identity, i.e. a pair consisting of a morphism $\varepsilon_1 : \operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ together with a proof that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $c$ is the identity — a section of $c$. Let $m \ge 1$ be a natural number, let $V$ be an open subset of $C$ which is an affine open, assume every point in the range of the underlying map of $\varepsilon_1$ lies in $V$, and let $g \in \Gamma(C, V)$ be a section such that for every affine open $W$ of $C$ with $W \le V$, the component at $W$ of the ideal sheaf data $(\ker \varepsilon_1)^m$ is the ideal of $\Gamma(C, W)$ generated by the restriction of $g$ to $W$. Equip $\Gamma(C, V)$ with the $R$-algebra structure coming from $c$, namely the ring map $(\Gamma\mathrm{Spec}\text{-iso})^{-1}$ followed by $c.\mathrm{appLE}\,\top\,V$. Then the quotient $\Gamma(C, V) / (g)$ is a finite $R$-module, and for every field $L$ in universe $u$ equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, $\dim_L \bigl(L \otimes_R \Gamma(C, V)/(g)\bigr) = m$.
--
--   This is the affine-chart form of the statement that the $m$-th infinitesimal neighbourhood $m\varepsilon$ of a section of a smooth proper relative curve is finite flat of degree $m$ over the base, recorded in the base-change-stable form 'finite over $R$, of dimension $m$ over every field over $R$' rather than 'free of rank $m$', so that it applies over a general Noetherian base. It feeds the construction of two-chart pole data, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_twoChartPoleDatum_forall_finrank_of_section_invModule`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_twoChartPoleDatum_forall_finrank_of_section_invModule).
